      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DANGEROUS (10) makes his first appearance since July's Inter Dominion series where he won a heat and was fourth in the final. Readied with two trials, winning the latest, and has won five of eight fresh attempts. Draws widest but is good enough to overcome that. SPRINGFIELD AFFAIR (1) has been a revelation in winning all four starts over this distance since joining Seaton Grima, last week overcoming a wide draw to get home by 2m. This is stronger but he led from this barrier to score well prior so can give a big sight again. RAKERO ROCKET NZ (7) is much better than what he showed first up. That was his first outing for nearly six months so he should be better for it. Worth another chance. NYACK (9) was first up for eight weeks when runner-up to an in-form rival last start. Draws wider but should be fitter and beat DANGEROUS when he placed in the Inter Dominion final two back.",
